{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff state. Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2536 (\"Derive create's ticket-type vocabulary\"). Gate state at handoff: LLM-Review +1, Verified -1 — the code review PASSED and only CI is red.\n\nTwo failure signatures are open across this stack and neither root cause is confirmed yet:\n1. change 2530 fails the `require resolvable rebar ticket` job, although `rebar resolve` succeeds locally and the trailer is well-formed — the leading hypothesis is that the ticket is not visible to CI (the `tickets` branch may not have reached `origin`);\n2. pytest fails in ~50s on several changes, fast enough to be a collection/import error, and it does NOT reproduce locally.\n\nDo NOT close this ticket until its change is Verified +1 and merged. A subagent is driving the stack to green; a session-only cron loop (46e3b0eb) is harvesting reviews, landing green changes and closing merged tickets.\n\nNote for whoever lands this: amend only with `git commit --amend --no-edit`. Re-committing a change that already carries a Change-Id opens a DUPLICATE Gerrit change — that is how change 2534 came to exist and be abandoned."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788398763289796001,"uuid":"b6973b70-321c-41ba-b7b7-a6001f340355"}